Key judgment calls: Unit 2 and Unit 7 each had two defensible splits (a minimal fix and one that further splits at a real subordinator/coordinator), so both were accepted with the more thorough one chosen. Unit 5's `c01` was rejected despite fixing the reported findings because it would leave two full sentences ("...correctly." / "In") fused onto one line — the same defect the rule targets, just unreported for that specific line. Unit 8 required picking the sole candidate resolving *both* fused findings without severing an invalid list-comma/list-"and"; the leftover 120+-char lines are the advisory `long` finding, which has no valid nearby boundary to split at (the list commas/"and" are excluded by the "A, B, and C" rule) so were correctly left alone.
